<section class="article-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Translation guide</span><h1>Live Captions Translation for Chrome Audio</h1><p>Use Audicap to turn Chrome tab audio into live captions and translated text while videos, courses, podcasts, webinars, or meetings are still playing.</p><div class="article-meta"><span>Updated May 16, 2026</span><span>6 minute read</span></div></div></section>
<section class="article-layout">
<div class="container article-shell">
<article class="article-body">
<h2>Quick Answer</h2>
<p>Live captions translation means converting spoken audio into text and translating it as the audio plays. With Audicap, this happens from the current Chrome tab, so it can help with YouTube lectures, online courses, podcasts, webinars, Google Meet, Zoom web, and other regular browser audio.</p>
<p>It is most useful when you need to understand the main ideas quickly, not when you need a certified translation or perfectly edited transcript.</p>
<h2>Best Use Cases</h2>
<ul><li>Watching a YouTube lecture in another language.</li><li>Following an online course taught by a non-native speaker.</li><li>Understanding a webinar or podcast with technical vocabulary.</li><li>Joining an international Google Meet or Zoom web call.</li><li>Reviewing translated notes after a training session.</li></ul>
<h2>How Live Translation Works In Audicap</h2>
<ol><li>Open the video, meeting, course, or podcast in Chrome.</li><li>Click the Audicap toolbar icon.</li><li>Start live transcription for the current tab.</li><li>Enable translation and choose the target language.</li><li>Read the transcript and translated text during playback.</li><li>Export or share the transcript when the session ends.</li></ol>
<h2>Live Translation Compared With Manual Workflows</h2>
<table class="comparison-table">
<tr><th>Workflow</th><th>Best for</th><th>Limitation</th></tr>
<tr><td>Manual pause and translate</td><td>Short clips and individual phrases.</td><td>Slow and disruptive for long videos.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Uploaded file transcription</td><td>Pre-recorded files you already have.</td><td>Requires downloading or uploading content first.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Chrome tab live translation</td><td>Videos, courses, podcasts, webinars, and meetings while they play.</td><td>Depends on audio quality and browser capture permissions.</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>Tips For Better Results</h2>
<ul><li>Use clear source audio when possible.</li><li>Avoid playing multiple audio sources in the same tab.</li><li>Review important translated notes after the session.</li><li>Use summaries to extract key points from longer transcripts.</li><li>Export the transcript if you need to study or share it later.</li></ul>
<div class="article-callout"><h3>Try live translation in Chrome</h3><p>New users get 30 free minutes. Translate Chrome tab audio live and export the transcript when you are done.</p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/audicap/cfalkkjbhiohkomajlelefmllnoniloo?utm_source=audicap_website&amp;utm_medium=seo&amp;utm_campaign=live_captions_translation">Add Audicap to Chrome</a></div>
<h2>FAQ</h2>
<div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Can I translate YouTube audio live?</summary><p>Yes. Open the YouTube video in Chrome, start Audicap live transcription, and enable translation for the target language.</p></details><details><summary>Can I save the translated transcript?</summary><p>Audicap is designed for transcript review, export, and sharing after a live session. Export availability depends on the current transcript state and selected format.</p></details><details><summary>Does this work on desktop app audio?</summary><p>No. Audicap captures audio from regular Chrome tabs. Desktop app audio is outside the Chrome tab capture workflow.</p></details></div>
<h2>Related Guides</h2>
<p>For YouTube workflows, read <a href="/use-cases/youtube-transcript-generator">YouTube transcript generator for Chrome</a>. For meetings, see <a href="/blog/transcribe-google-meet-without-bot">Google Meet transcription without a bot</a> and <a href="/blog/transcribe-zoom-web">Zoom web transcription in Chrome</a>.</p>
</article>
